Med:19405910). Acts as a coactivator (with NCOA2) of the androgen receptor (AR)-mediated transactivation (PubMed:17587566). Acts as a coactivator (with estrogen) of estrogen receptor (ER)-mediated transactivation (PubMed:12039952). Enhances PGR, PPARG, RARA-mediated transactivation (PubMed:12039952). May inhibit NF-kappa-B transcription and promote apoptosis (PubMed:16648481). Represses E2F1 transcriptional activity (in a RB1-dependent manner) (By similarity). May be involved in growth regulation (By similarity). Involved in PRMT2IP-mediated inhibition of the microglial inflammatory responses through suppression of NF-kappa-B signaling, thereby reducing the production of pro-inflammatory cytokines (PubMed:38892217)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}